{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": "Tune26 T26-4: a local certified bool[] proves its plain unshared carrier once before same-lane stores and reads. Each guarded access keeps its dynamic bounds checks and the checked setter as the cold miss path; an alias remains observable as a COW snapshot. 2026-09-13: the checked path is now array_num_set_cow_idx (CW32v2), the raw bool load folds its element offset into the computed address instead of a u8:3 displacement, and the group is scoped to the proven region -- the guarded `while` emits a generic sibling (D2.2.2, D8.3.1) whose own raw load would otherwise be counted as a third. The two inlined u8 certificate reads are gone on purpose: CW32v2 tests the shared bit at operation entry inside array_num_set_cow_idx, so the sequence now pins what the same-lane store still guarantees -- a bounds check against the length, then the raw u8 lane store through the data pointer. 2026-09-17 (T28-7): the first pinned store is `flags[0]`, whose literal index is now proven non-negative, so its negative-index test is gone; the length test remains because `fill(n + 1, ...)` has no static length.",
  "checks": [
    {
      "in_func": "_tune26_same_owner_store_#",
      "expect_seq": [
        "mov\t{{r}}, i64:40({{r}})",
        "ge\t{{r}}, {{r}}, {{r}}",
        "mov\t{{r}}, i64:32({{r}})",
        "mul\t{{r}}, {{r}}, 1",
        "mov\tu8:({{r}}), {{r}}"
      ],
      "expect": [
        "call\tarray_num_set_cow_idx"
      ],
      "count": {
        "mov\t{{r}}, u8:({{r}})": 2
      },
      "in_range": {
        "from": "func\t",
        "to": "ne\t{{r}}, {{r}}, -9223372036854775808"
      }
    }
  ]
}
